Two fixes to potx' @Translation annotation extractor.

Both are filed upstream as
https://www.drupal.org/project/potx/issues/3615813. They are in the same
patch because they are in the same function, a few lines apart, so applying
one without the other means resolving a conflict. If the maintainers would
rather have the second one on its own issue, this patch splits again along
the numbered sections below.

1. Extract annotations that carry an arguments parameter.

The annotation pattern only allowed an optional "context" parameter after the
string, then required the closing parenthesis. Any other parameter made the
match fail, so the string was not extracted at all - and potx then reported it
as "In @Translation, only one, non-empty static string is allowed in double
quotes", which is misleading since the syntax is valid.

The common case is "arguments", used for placeholders:

  description = @Translation("A string provided by <a href=':google'>Google</a>.",
    arguments = { ":google" = "https://www.google.com/" }),

Both "arguments" and "context" are documented parameters of the Translation
annotation, so this is a genuine upstream bug rather than a local need. In our
codebase it cost the Danish translations of roughly a dozen metatag field
descriptions.

The replacement allows any number of "key = value" parameters on either side of
an optional context, and keeps the capture group numbering the code below
depends on: 1 is the message, 3 is the quoted context.

2. Escape what the extractor found.

Potx normally escapes what it extracts before handing it on -
_potx_format_quoted_string() is called in 22 places in potx.inc, and turns
control characters into their escape sequences. The annotation extractor is
the exception: it passes its raw regex match straight to the save callback.

An annotation wrapped over two lines therefore arrives with a real newline and
the doc comment's continuation in it:

  description = @Translation("Sends emails through an external
  service")

Written to a .po file as-is that is not a .po file at all - gettext reports
"end-of-line within string" and throws away every term in the file, not just
the one string. A single wrapped annotation anywhere in the scanned code takes
the whole translation file with it.

Escaping is also what keeps the msgid usable. Drupal's own annotation parser
keeps the newline and the " * " continuation, so the escaped string is the one
that gets looked up at runtime; an unwrapped, tidied-up msgid would read better
and never match.

_potx_format_quoted_string() is not the right tool here even though it is what
the other extractors use. It runs stripcslashes() first, which is correct for
PHP string literals but not for annotations - Doctrine does not read backslash
escapes, so a literal "\n" in an annotation would become a real newline and the
msgid would stop matching. The pattern above cannot capture a quote either, so
addcslashes() on its own covers everything that can occur.

diff --git a/potx.inc b/potx.inc
--- a/potx.inc
+++ b/potx.inc
@@ -2307,12 +2307,30 @@
       // Match for a possible empty string too, so we can signal that kind of
       // error in our standard way (from the save callback), instead of
       // signaling a generic error from here around syntax.
-      preg_match_all('!\s*@Translation\(\s*"([^"]*)"(\s*,\s*context\s*=\s*("[^"]+"))?\s*\)!', $string, $found);
+      // Annotations may carry parameters besides context - most commonly
+      // arguments, used for placeholders in for example metatag descriptions.
+      // Allow any number of those on either side of an optional context, so
+      // that the string is still extracted. The delimiter is "~" rather than
+      // "!" because the negative lookahead below contains "!".
+      $other_parameter = '(?:\s*,\s*(?!context\s*=)[a-zA-Z_]+\s*=\s*(?:\{[^{}]*\}|"[^"]*"))';
+      $pattern = '~\s*@Translation\(\s*"([^"]*)"'
+        . $other_parameter . '*'
+        . '(\s*,\s*context\s*=\s*("[^"]+"))?'
+        . $other_parameter . '*'
+        . '\s*\)~';
+      preg_match_all($pattern, $string, $found);
       if (isset($found) && is_array($found) && count($found[1])) {
 
         foreach ($found[1] as $index => $match) {
           $context = empty($found[3][$index]) ? POTX_CONTEXT_NONE : trim($found[3][$index], '"');
 
+          // Escape the raw match, the way every other extractor does through
+          // _potx_format_quoted_string(). That function itself is not usable
+          // here: it starts with stripcslashes(), which is right for a PHP
+          // string literal but not for an annotation, where Doctrine leaves
+          // backslash escapes alone.
+          $match = addcslashes($match, "\0..\37\\\"");
+
           $save_callback(
             $match,
             $context,
